    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-11T09:20:14+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T09:20:14+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T22:50:14Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T22:50:14Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak ridge of high pressure develops south of Bight today. This ridge will persist into Thursday before a broad area of low pressure develops over SA on Friday. This low will track eastwards, making way for a new high pressure ridge in the west on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 25 to 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. Slight chance of a shower in the evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Light winds becoming north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending west to northwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm on and east of the ranges in the morning. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
